1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,175
Every place has a story. But the people who share a street can experience it very differently.

2
00:00:06,458 --> 00:00:15,647
Kiez Notes explores how those everyday perspectives can become new narratives of a place—a shared narrative
told by the people who are there.

3
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:25,350
Start with the map, choose a neighborhood, and open its shared page. Residents, newcomers and visitors can all
read.

4
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:34,093
To leave a written or spoken note, you confirm your location and choose a nickname. There are no accounts,
profiles, likes or followers.

5
00:00:34,375 --> 00:00:40,594
Think of it as a wiki-style page for a place. No single person owns what it says.

6
00:00:40,875 --> 00:00:48,426
Each new note goes on top of a stack and replaces the visible moment. Only today’s latest note appears.

7
00:00:48,708 --> 00:00:53,969
Earlier notes remain stored beneath it, ready to become part of the neighborhood’s memory.

8
00:00:54,250 --> 00:01:04,207
Past days take a different form. The Chronicle pipeline gathers a day’s notes into one summarized story, narrated
as “I,” the neighborhood.

9
00:01:04,458 --> 00:01:14,128
The aim is to preserve different moods and uncertainty: a lively canal can feel welcoming to one person and
overwhelming to another.

10
00:01:14,417 --> 00:01:21,160
These Chronicles form the archive. Empty days receive no invented story.

11
00:01:21,417 --> 00:01:24,979
People don’t need to share a language to share a place.

12
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:33,689
Spoken notes become transcripts that contributors review and edit before publishing. Original text and language
are preserved.

13
00:01:33,958 --> 00:01:40,881
Readers can request translation or speech in English, German, Turkish, Arabic and Spanish.

14
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:49,548
Gemini supports these language and voice features; OpenAI powers Chronicle extraction, writing and review.

15
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:55,091
The prototype covers four Berlin neighborhoods and Hamburg’s HafenCity.

16
00:01:55,375 --> 00:02:06,108
The demo archive contains labeled editorial stories; live Chronicle generation has been rehearsed, with grounding
and daily scheduling still to improve.

17
00:02:06,375 --> 00:02:17,840
Kiez Notes brings together a changing present and a shared memory. Explore the project, and imagine what story
your neighborhood could tell.
